From caafb4daebf9df611d6e0ebbf3fb1ae028e62661 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Analyser <analyser@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:24:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(coding-agent): opt-in package namespace (pi.namespace)
 for skills and prompt templates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem: pi loads package skills and prompt templates into flat name-keyed
maps; a package resource named foo collides with any same-named user/project
resource (first-found-wins + warning). Package authors work around it by
baking prefixes into SKILL.md frontmatter or naming template files with
literal colons, forking resources from their upstream or cross-harness form.

Solution: an opt-in per-package declaration, pi.namespace in package.json.
Skills load as <ns>:<name> (invoked /skill:<ns>:<name>, or the bare
/<ns>:<name> when no template owns the name — templates keep precedence);
prompt templates as /<ns>:<name>. The colon never enters resource content:
the prefix composes at load time, before collision dedupe, so namespaced and
same-named bare resources coexist. Bare base-name invocations keep resolving
via a unique-owner fallback (never for colon-bearing or ambiguous requests).

- pi-manifest: parse pi.namespace; ResourceArrayKey narrows resource lookups
- package-manager: carry namespace on PathMetadata (single manifest read)
- skills/prompt-templates loaders: namespaces option, rename-at-load,
  validateNamespaceValue, findNamespaceForPath, findSkillByInvocationName,
  resolveBareNamespaceSkill
- resource-loader: build validated associations from package-origin
  metadata; invalid values warn into the owning diagnostics channel
- agent-session: /skill: expansion via findSkillByInvocationName; bare
  namespace-form resolution wired between skill and template expansion
- interactive autocomplete: namespaced skills also surface under the bare
  /<ns>:<name> form when no template owns the composed name
- docs: skills.md, packages.md, prompt-templates.md

Boundary semantics, all regression-tested: raw settings/CLI paths into a
package load bare; --extension <pkg-dir> skills load bare (the cli restamp
loop pre-empts package metadata) while prompts compose (no restamp loop
exists for prompts); dual resolution keeps the package registration
(composed). Themes are not namespaced (startup resolution bypasses the
loader registry); runtime-registered tools/commands are untouched.

Out of scope: themes, runtime registrations, settings-level overrides.
